red out; finished in 0.59s\ntest result: ok. 30 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.83s\ntest result: ok. 39 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.39s\ntest result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.02s\ntest result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xf43a3qqct6jiytcpmssx3exrkivko5g2h22ykebupif3jkytyyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases done, every gate independently verified.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a cut-down `cute_c2` 2-D collision library: vector math, a GJK distance solver with a warm-start cache, six boolean shape predicates, a dispatcher, and one entry point in `lib.h` (`capsule`). The C `.so` exports **all 38** non-`static` functions, so all 38 are the ABI under test.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 38 `nm -D` symbols; parity table for debug **and** release Rust `.so`; build-config surface |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 60-row error-surface table, one row per distinct rejection grepped from the C |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 71-row configuration-surface table (the option × input-shape cross-product) |\n\n**Feature matrix:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `c_src` has no `#if`/`#ifdef` — exactly one configuration. `cargo check` is clean for `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features` (`--all-targets`, zero warnings). Since features couldn't vary, I varied the axis that could: the suite runs against the **debug and release** cdylib.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\n- **71/71** `CONFIGS.md` rows and **60/60** `ERRORS.md` rows pass — 113 tests, **7,222,349** bit-exact comparisons, all through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s (Rust is never called directly).\n- Symbol diff is **empty** (38/38) in both profiles; no missing implementations, so no C source needed translating.\n- Measured branch coverage, not assumed: all 3 `c22` branches, all 7 `c23` branches, all 3 `c2CircletoCapsule` branches, all 8 `capsule()` return values, 4 of 5 GJK loop guards.\n\n## Four findings worth your attention\n\n1. **NaN payload bits are the one tolerated difference.** GCC and LLVM pick different destination registers for commutative `mulss`/`addss`, and x86 returns the *destination's* NaN. I disassembled both to confirm. IEEE-754 §6.2.3 leaves this unspecified, and no Rust source spelling can pin GCC's register allocation. So NaN-*ness* is compared strictly, all non-NaN values bit-exactly, and only mutually-NaN payloads are tolerated — counted and printed per row.\n\n2. **Three `ERRORS.md` rows are unbounded UB where the C itself faults**, which I found by running them: an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` leaves `pA.count` uninitialised and it becomes `c2Support`'s loop bound (SIGSEGV); `cache->count >= 4` writes past `saveA[3]`/`saveB[3]` and smashes `c2GJK`'s own frame (SIGSEGV). There is no behaviour to match, so I assert the well-defined observable part instead and document the rest rather than pretending it passed.\n\n3. **Two rows are provably unreachable**, not untested: the 20-iteration cap (max reachable is 5, since ≤4-vertex proxies make `dup` fire first) and the `NaN`-truthiness arm of the two GJK-backed predicates (`use_radius != 0` forces `dist = 0`). Both are replaced by the strongest checkable assertion.\n\n4. **I found and fixed two harness defects that would have produced false passes.** `cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`-only library, so the suite was loading a stale `.so` — a `c2Skew` mutation went undetected. Fixed via `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]`, newest-artifact selection (cargo only *uplifts* on `cargo build`), and a hard staleness assertion. `mutation_check.sh` also counted a crashing mutant as \"not caught\".\n\n`./mutation_check.sh` now injects 20 plausible translation slips and catches **20/20**, including the tempting \"fix\" of the C's swapped `AABB × CIRCLE` operands in `c2Collided` — evidence the suite isn't vacuous. Two mutants I initially wrote turned out to be genuinely equivalent (documented, replaced). `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to before the battery, and `c_src/` is unmodified (md5 verified)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1135,"cache_read_input_tokens":335309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1135,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8842cf7-2421-4bd3-8295-9778a8790a6e","uuid":"af88edf0-74cc-461a-8f5d-abe2dd9c8b35","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:50:38.811Z"}
