o harness defects that would have produced false passes.** `cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`-only library, so the suite was loading a stale `.so` — a `c2Skew` mutation went undetected. Fixed via `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]`, newest-artifact selection (cargo only *uplifts* on `cargo build`), and a hard staleness assertion. `mutation_check.sh` also counted a crashing mutant as \"not caught\".\n\n`./mutation_check.sh` now injects 20 plausible translation slips and catches **20/20**, including the tempting \"fix\" of the C's swapped `AABB × CIRCLE` operands in `c2Collided` — evidence the suite isn't vacuous. Two mutants I initially wrote turned out to be genuinely equivalent (documented, replaced). `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to before the battery, and `c_src/` is unmodified (md5 verified).","ttft_ms":2324,"ttft_stream_ms":1923,"time_to_request_ms":38,"type":"result","duration_ms":2749005,"uuid":"3ce8a0bc-7dbd-4a47-a076-ccaa2b0e2682"}
